ty of which  was coming from  that dinner meal her date also came in  as  pretty low carb high fat and on the  lower end of the recommended protein  range she was also low on most of her  micronutrients  but most notably for a young woman of  her age  calcium and iron and also there weren't  any major sources of omega-3s  in her diet so let me start by giving  the girl credit  where credit is due olivia seems to have  a  pretty laid-back approach to food she  admits that she's  not the most adventurous eater and she  prefers things to be kind of bland  and plain and that might explain the  repetitiveness  of some of these ingredients but i'm  just happy that i didn't hear any  explicit demonizing of foods  wellness misinformation or an obsession  with clean eating  she doesn't seem to like cut out any  food groups or  or the typically off-limit foods like  cheese and bread  and she also isn't consuming massive  bowls of lettuce  like it's her day job she just kind of  seems like she's eating what she likes  and for the most part her meals seem  pretty accessible  and simple but let's talk a little bit  about some gentle nutrition tips  first of all i would just kind of love  to see  more food throughout the day i don't  know for sure if this is olivia's  typical dietary pattern but  i don't know it seems like she eats  pretty light all day long  and then eats half of her day's calories  at dinner  so i would love to see a few more  balanced snacks  peppered throughout the day just to  ensure that she's better able to meet  her micronutrient needs for the day  and also keep her energy levels steady  so ideally we would want to be thinking  about the hunger  crushing combo and building these snacks  and meals  so that means of course a source of  fiber protein  and healthy fats so this could mean  maybe adding some  guacamole hummus or like a white bean  dip  with her veggie chips combining a couple  hard-boiled eggs with some crackers and  cheese  or making a really 